{{!-- Ghost renders navigation through the {{navigation}} helper, and the helper is
      what puts the list into scope: a {{#foreach navigation}} written anywhere else
      iterates nothing and fails silently, which is exactly how the About link and
      the footer links went missing. Overriding this partial is how a theme keeps its
      own markup -- bare <a> elements, no <ul>, because .nav and .foot-links lay their
      children out directly.

      Both lists arrive here. `isSecondary` tells them apart, and only the primary
      one marks the current page: the footer is a list of elsewheres. --}}
{{#foreach navigation}}
  {{#if ../isSecondary}}<a href="{{url}}">{{> icon}}{{label}}</a>
  {{else}}<a href="{{url}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}}</a>
  {{/if}}
{{/foreach}}
